		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=18387#p18387"><![CDATA[
Hello for everybody!<br>We are an independent (creative, design, dj, developer..) team called <span style="color:#FF8040">EMBERGEP</span> (it means Manmachine). We've created a minimal-design space adventure game called <span style="color:#FFBF40">Spacework</span>. We are using Bullet Physics in it. It works fine <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"><br><br>If you like design product, arcade &amp; old-school style, retro style, tech style and minimal stuffs, you will like the style of our first game.<br>We are very excited about Spacework and if everything will goes fine, we want to create a second part <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"> <br><br>You and your space team is attacked by robots, and you are the only one who survives. The attackers take you and your ship to their planet, the Triton and leave you alone in a zone under control. You need to find and regain the Monolith. Then leave the planet and go to Titan... The second part will start from here...<br><br>The game site: <a href="http://www.spaceworkgame.com" class="postlink">Spaceworkgame.com</a><br>It's available for Win and Mac OS X too.<br><br><a href="http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2MTLyMKqluk" class="postlink">Trailer on Youtube</a><br><a href="http://vimeo.com/8820351" class="postlink">Trailer on Vimeo</a><br><br>And if you like its music:<br><a href="http://www.myspace.com/spaceworkgame" class="postlink">myspace music</a><br><br>We hope you will like it and <span style="color:#80BFFF">let</span> <span style="color:#0040FF">us</span> <span style="color:#FF8040">know</span> how much  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":)" title="Smile"> <br>Have a good time!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6601">tefnerk</a> — Thu Apr 29, 2010 9:27 am</p><hr />
